{"id":"m1-04-s4","title":"Stage 4: Chirp at 100k users","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: caching strategies cache-aside, write-through, write-back, CDN for media, read replicas and replication lag. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"load-and-goal","title":"Load and goal","html":"<p><strong>Stage 4: about 100,000 users.</strong> Now the database is the bottleneck. Goal: protect Postgres from repeated reads using a cache, a CDN and read replicas, while keeping answers correct enough.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 100k users, 30% DAU = 30,000 DAU. Each loads the timeline 20 times and views 40 profiles/posts: about 60 reads per user a day = 1.8M reads/day = about 21 reads/s average, peak 5x = about 105 reads/s. Writes: 1.5 posts per DAU = 45k posts/day = 0.5 writes/s. Read:write is about 40:1. A timeline query joins 100 followees' posts and costs maybe 15 ms of DB CPU; 105 x 15 ms = 1.6 cores busy at peak on a 2-core DB. The DB is saturated, though the traffic looks tiny.</p>\n<p>Media: 20% of posts have an image of 300 KB = 9,000 images/day = 2.7 GB/day of new media; viewing multiplies it: 30,000 DAU x 30 images x 150 KB = 135 GB/day egress.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 585.6 192\" width=\"585.6\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Stage 4: cache, CDN and a read replica take load off the primary\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 96 L158 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 65 L304 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 65 L304 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 96 L158 127\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 127\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 127 L304 127\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 127 L304 127\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M407.2 127 L463.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M407.2 127 L463.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M407.2 127 L463.2 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M407.2 127 L463.2 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M407.2 127 L463.2 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M407.2 127 L463.2 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Users</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">CDN</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"105\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"131\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">ALB</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"43\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"355.6\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">S3 media</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"105\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"355.6\" y=\"131\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">App servers</text><rect x=\"463.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"518.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Redis cache</text><rect x=\"463.2\" y=\"74\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"518.4\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Primary DB</text><rect x=\"463.2\" y=\"136\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"518.4\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Read replica</text></svg><figcaption>Stage 4: cache, CDN and a read replica take load off the primary</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Facebook's memcache paper described the same pattern at planet scale; Twitter cached timelines in Redis; Instagram cached nearly everything in memcached in front of Postgres.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> The librarian keeps the most requested books on the desk (cache), makes photocopies for a second reading room (replica), and prints posters at the town square (CDN).</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\"Just add a cache\" without saying what is cached, key design, TTL and invalidation.</li>\n<li>Thinking read replicas help with writes. They do not.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"configuration","title":"Configuration","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Value</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>App servers</td>\n<td>4 x <code>c6i.large</code> (2 vCPU, 4 GB), ASG min 3 max 8, target CPU 55%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Redis</td>\n<td>ElastiCache Redis 7, <code>cache.m6g.large</code> (13 GB) primary + 1 replica, Multi-AZ, <code>maxmemory-policy allkeys-lru</code>, no persistence (cache only)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Primary DB</td>\n<td>RDS <code>db.r6g.xlarge</code> (4 vCPU, 32 GB), Multi-AZ, 200 GB gp3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Read replicas</td>\n<td>1 x <code>db.r6g.xlarge</code> (async), second one added when replica CPU above 60%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CDN</td>\n<td>CloudFront in front of S3 <code>chirp-media</code>, origin access control, HTTP/2 + brotli, price class 100</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CDN TTLs</td>\n<td>Immutable media keys (<code>img/{hash}.webp</code>): <code>Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable</code>; avatar URLs versioned</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>PgBouncer</td>\n<td>Transaction mode, <code>default_pool_size=40</code>, <code>max_client_conn=2000</code> (sits between 8 app instances and DB)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pools</td>\n<td>HikariCP 10 per app x 8 max, funnelled through PgBouncer</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Cache keys and TTLs:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Key</th>\n<th>Value</th>\n<th>TTL</th>\n<th>Strategy</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>user:{id}</code></td>\n<td>profile JSON</td>\n<td>10 min + 0 to 60 s jitter</td>\n<td>cache-aside</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>post:{id}</code></td>\n<td>post JSON</td>\n<td>1 h (posts rarely change)</td>\n<td>cache-aside</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>tl:{userId}</code></td>\n<td>list of 300 post ids</td>\n<td>60 s</td>\n<td>cache-aside, rebuilt on miss</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>fc:{userId}</code></td>\n<td>follower count</td>\n<td>none (kept by counter)</td>\n<td>write-through</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>likes:{postId}</code></td>\n<td>like counter</td>\n<td>flushed every 5 s</td>\n<td>write-back (see branch 4C)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Redis config:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">maxmemory</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> 10gb</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">maxmemory-policy</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> allkeys-lru</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">timeout</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 300</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">tcp-keepalive</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 60</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">save</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> \"\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">            # cache only, no RDB snapshots</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Postgres replica settings: <code>hot_standby_feedback=on</code>, <code>max_standby_streaming_delay=30s</code>; alert when replica lag exceeds 5 s.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>No jitter on TTLs: thousands of keys expire in the same second and stampede the DB.</li>\n<li>Running Redis with persistence for a pure cache; it adds latency spikes (fork) for no benefit.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"decision-and-why","title":"Decision and why","html":"<p><strong>Decision 1: cache the right things.</strong> Cache what is read often and changes rarely: profiles, posts by id, timelines as id lists, follower counts. Do not cache the unique, one-off query. Rule: put the cache behind the <code>Repository</code> interface (Stage 1 pays off here), so services do not know it exists.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision 2: store ids in the timeline cache, not full posts.</strong> <code>tl:{userId}</code> is 300 ids (about 2.4 KB). Hydrate them with a <code>MGET post:{id}...</code>. One post is cached once and shared by all timelines; changing or deleting a post updates one key.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision 3: CDN for media.</strong> Images are the biggest bandwidth cost. Serving through CloudFront keeps traffic off the app and the origin and moves bytes closer to users (latency from 250 ms to 30 ms for distant users). Because file names include a content hash, cache never needs invalidation.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision 4: read replicas for what cache cannot absorb.</strong> Search, user profile edits' follow-ups, and timeline cache misses go to the replica. The primary is for writes and read-your-own-writes.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision 5: handle replication lag explicitly.</strong> Async replicas lag by milliseconds normally and seconds under load. If a user posts and the next request reads from the replica, their post is missing, which looks like a bug. Fix: after any write, route that user's reads to the primary for 5 s (store <code>last_write_ts</code> in the JWT claim or a Redis key <code>rw:{userId}</code> with TTL 5 s).</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 280.4 192\" width=\"280.4\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Read-your-writes routing\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 96 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 96 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 96 L158 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">App</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"213.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Redis rw key</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"213.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Primary</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"136\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"213.2\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Replica</text></svg><figcaption>Read-your-writes routing</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Facebook \"remote markers\" in their memcache design to avoid stale reads after write; Instagram had replicas lag incidents in the early Postgres days; Pinterest and GitHub use primary-for-recent-writes routing.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> After you edit a Google Doc, it shows you your own edit immediately even if other people see it a second later.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Sending every read to the replica including \"read your own post\". Users will report \"my post disappeared\".</li>\n<li>Caching entire timelines of full post objects: duplicated memory and impossible invalidation.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"alternatives-branches","title":"Alternatives (branches)","html":"<h3>Branch 4A: cache-aside (lazy loading) (chosen for most keys)</h3>\n<p>App checks cache; on miss reads DB and fills cache.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pros: only requested data is cached; cache failure only costs speed; simple.</li>\n<li>Cons: first read after expiry is slow; stale data until TTL or explicit delete; stampede risk.</li>\n<li>Mitigations: jitter TTL, request coalescing (singleflight: only one thread loads a key), serve-stale-while-revalidate, <code>DEL</code> key on update.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Branch 4B: write-through</h3>\n<p>Writes go to cache and DB together; reads always hit the cache.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pros: cache always fresh for keys written through it; good for follower counters and profile after edit.</li>\n<li>Cons: write latency doubles; caches data never read; failure between the two writes needs care (write DB first, then cache; on cache error just delete).</li>\n<li>Used for: <code>fc:{userId}</code> and profile updates.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Branch 4C: write-back (write-behind)</h3>\n<p>Writes hit the cache; DB is updated later asynchronously in batches.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pros: absorbs write bursts; hot counters (likes on a viral post) turn 10,000 DB writes/s into one per 5 s.</li>\n<li>Cons: <strong>data loss if Redis dies before flush</strong>; hard to debug.</li>\n<li>Chosen only for like/view counters where losing 5 s of counts is acceptable. Never for posts, follows, or money.</li>\n</ul>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Likes: INCR likes:{post}  ->  every 5 s a flusher does</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  UPDATE posts SET like_count = like_count + :delta   (batched)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Loss window: up to 5 s of counter increments</span></span></code></pre>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>cache-aside</th>\n<th>write-through</th>\n<th>write-back</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Write path</td>\n<td>DB only (delete key)</td>\n<td>DB + cache</td>\n<td>cache only</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Read freshness</td>\n<td>stale until TTL</td>\n<td>fresh</td>\n<td>fresh</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Data-loss risk</td>\n<td>none</td>\n<td>none</td>\n<td>yes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Best for</td>\n<td>profiles, posts, timelines</td>\n<td>counters needing consistency</td>\n<td>hot counters</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 564 68\" width=\"564\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Cache-aside read\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M108 34 L164 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M108 34 L164 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M254 34 L310 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M254 34 L310 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M400 34 L456 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M400 34 L456 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">App server</text><rect x=\"164\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"209\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Redis</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"355\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Miss</text><rect x=\"456\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"504\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Replica DB</text></svg><figcaption>Cache-aside read</figcaption></figure>\n<h3>Replication choices</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Async (chosen): fast writes, lag possible.</li>\n<li>Synchronous (<code>synchronous_commit=remote_apply</code>): no lag but a replica outage blocks writes. Rejected for Chirp.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>CDN choices</h3>\n<p>CloudFront (chosen, same cloud, simple), Cloudflare (cheaper egress, strong DDoS), Fastly (instant purge). All reversible.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Facebook and Twitter use look-aside (cache-aside) for reads; Redis <code>INCR</code> plus periodic flush is how many sites do view counters; Netflix Open Connect places CDN boxes inside ISPs.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Cache-aside is checking the fridge and shopping only when empty; write-through is stocking the fridge every time you buy; write-back is writing receipts at the end of the week.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Picking write-back for important data.</li>\n<li>Forgetting cache stampede and \"thundering herd\" on a viral key; also forgetting \"negative caching\" for missing users.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"what-breaks-next","title":"What breaks next","html":"<ol>\n<li><strong>Hot keys</strong>: one celebrity profile gets 5,000 reads/s on a single Redis key and a single shard.</li>\n<li><strong>Slow image uploads and processing</strong> are done inside the request: a 4 MB upload resized in-process takes 800 ms and blocks threads. Metric: p99 of <code>POST /posts</code> above 2 s.</li>\n<li><strong>Notifications and emails</strong> are sent synchronously; an SMTP hiccup fails the post request.</li>\n<li><strong>Primary write load and size</strong>: 200 GB and growing; vacuum and backups slow down.</li>\n<li><strong>Replica lag spikes</strong> during bulk jobs.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 656.4 68\" width=\"656.4\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Heavy work should leave the request path\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M122.4 34 L178.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M122.4 34 L178.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M288.8 34 L344.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M288.8 34 L344.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M498.4 34 L554.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M498.4 34 L554.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"67.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Post request</text><rect x=\"178.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"233.60000000000002\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Resize image</text><rect x=\"344.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"153.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"421.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Send notifications</text><rect x=\"554.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"599.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Respond</text></svg><figcaption>Heavy work should leave the request path</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Not naming the next bottleneck. Here it is synchronous side work, so the answer is a queue (Stage 5).</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"cost","title":"Cost","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Monthly</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>4 x <code>c6i.large</code></td>\n<td>about $250</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>ALB</td>\n<td>about $40</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>RDS primary <code>db.r6g.xlarge</code> Multi-AZ</td>\n<td>about $740</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1 read replica <code>db.r6g.xlarge</code></td>\n<td>about $370</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>DB storage 200 GB x 3 copies</td>\n<td>about $60</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>ElastiCache <code>cache.m6g.large</code> x 2</td>\n<td>about $290</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>PgBouncer on 2 small VMs</td>\n<td>about $30</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CloudFront (about 4 TB at $0.085 per GB; free tier covers 1 TB)</td>\n<td>about $250</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>S3 (1 TB storage, requests)</td>\n<td>about $40</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Logs, monitoring, transfer</td>\n<td>about $120</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Total</strong></td>\n<td><strong>about $2,190 per month</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>About $0.02 per user per month; cost per user falls as the cache and CDN bite.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Forgetting CDN egress: a viral image can cost more than the servers.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"lld-view","title":"LLD view","html":"<p>The repository layer gets a decorator, and read routing becomes explicit.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>PostRepository (interface)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  ├─ PostgresPostRepository   (SQL)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  └─ CachedPostRepository     (decorator: Redis in front, delegates on miss)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>DataSourceRouter: WRITE -> primary, READ -> replica, READ_AFTER_WRITE -> primary (5 s window)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>CounterService: INCR in Redis, scheduled flusher (with lock) to Postgres</span></span></code></pre>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">class</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> CachedPostRepository</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    private</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> val</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> delegate: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">PostRepository</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    private</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> val</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> redis: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">RedisClient</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) : </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">PostRepository</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    override</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> fun</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> findById</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(id: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">Long</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">): </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">Post</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">? {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">        redis.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">get</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"post:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">$id</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)?.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">let</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">return</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> json.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">decode</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(it) }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">        val</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> p </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> delegate.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">findById</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(id) ?: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">return</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> null</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">also</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { redis.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">setex</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"post:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">$id</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">30</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"NULL\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) } </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// negative cache</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">        redis.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">setex</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"post:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">$id</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">3600</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> +</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Random.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">nextInt</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">60</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">), json.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">encode</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(p))</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">        return</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> p</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    override</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> fun</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> save</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(post: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">Post</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">): </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">Post</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> =</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> delegate.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">save</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(post).</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">also</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { redis.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">del</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"post:${it.id}\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">}</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>This is the <strong>decorator pattern</strong>: callers still depend on <code>PostRepository</code>. Routing uses a thread-local \"consistency\" hint set by the service (<code>@Transactional(readOnly = true)</code> maps to the replica).</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 606 130\" width=\"606\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Decorator keeps services unaware of cache\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M115.2 65 L171.2 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 65 L171.2 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M274.4 65 L330.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M274.4 65 L330.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M448 34 L504 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M448 34 L504 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M274.4 65 L330.4 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M274.4 65 L330.4 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"63.6\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">PostService</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"43\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"222.79999999999998\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Cached repo</text><rect x=\"330.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"389.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Postgres repo</text><rect x=\"330.4\" y=\"74\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"389.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Redis</text><rect x=\"504\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"549\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Postgres</text></svg><figcaption>Decorator keeps services unaware of cache</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Updating the cache and DB in the wrong order: write DB then delete cache; the reverse leaves stale data after a failed DB write.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"decision-gravity","title":"Decision gravity","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Decision</th>\n<th>Gravity</th>\n<th>Why</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Cache-aside with Redis</td>\n<td>Reversible</td>\n<td>Cache is disposable; turn it off and the DB is slower, not wrong</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Write-back for counters</td>\n<td>Reversible but data-loss-prone</td>\n<td>Accepts loss of a few seconds of counts</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Timeline cached as id lists</td>\n<td>Semi one-way</td>\n<td>Becomes the shape for fan-out design in later stages</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CDN</td>\n<td>Reversible</td>\n<td>Change DNS; cache-bust by key hash</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Content-hashed immutable media keys</td>\n<td><strong>One-way-ish</strong></td>\n<td>Everything (URLs in DB, caches) depends on the naming scheme</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Async replicas</td>\n<td>Reversible</td>\n<td>Can add sync later; app must tolerate lag</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Read/write routing in code</td>\n<td>Medium</td>\n<td>Hard to retrofit, easy to build behind the repository</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Treating cache invalidation as a detail. It is the hardest part and defines correctness.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"concepts-learned","title":"Concepts learned","html":"<ul>\n<li>Cache-aside, write-through, write-back and when each is safe.</li>\n<li>TTL jitter, stampede, negative caching, singleflight.</li>\n<li>CDN, immutable assets, content-hash URLs.</li>\n<li>Primary and read replicas, async replication, replication lag, read-your-writes.</li>\n<li>Connection pooler (PgBouncer) in transaction mode.</li>\n<li>Decorator pattern for caching.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Confusing a cache hit ratio target: aim for 90% plus; measure <code>keyspace_hits / (hits + misses)</code>.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>Stage 4 (about 100k users): Redis <code>cache.m6g.large</code> with TTLs 10 min to 1 h and jitter, CloudFront CDN for media, 1 read replica <code>db.r6g.xlarge</code>, PgBouncer; about $2,190 per month.</li>\n<li>Cache ids not objects; cache-aside for profiles/posts/timelines, write-through for follower counts, write-back only for like counters.</li>\n<li>Replicas are async: route a user's reads to the primary for 5 s after their write; alert on lag above 5 s.</li>\n<li>Behind the repository interface, use a decorator so services stay unchanged.</li>\n<li>Next bottleneck: heavy synchronous work (image resize, notifications) in the request path, so Stage 5 adds queues and workers.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}